 a vengeful verbose baby the  episode death has a shadow focuses a bit  more on peter and doesn't try to be  subtle early in the episode his defense  to keep lois from uncovering his lies is  to call her fat he loses his job due to  drinking 37 beers and brian hits him on  the head with a newspaper like he's the  bad dog all of this is in the first half  of the episode from there peta becomes  welfare rich flies a blimp over the  super bowl and lands in jail it's a lot  quite the journey for a main character  in a first outing the episode's central  conflict is finally resolved thanks to  stewie's mind control device but only  after the kool-aid man burst through a  wall oh yeah  the second episode i never met the dead  man holds a memorable moment for many  die hard fans one that lands somewhere  between ingenuity and insanity for those  who have forgotten that far back it's  peter's fault that the town has no cable  television and meg is taking the blame  for the incident to cope with not being  able to occupy his time in front of the  tube peter gets creative and crafts his  own set out of household scraps what  most might not remember about this  particular episode is that it features  the series first big celebrity cameo not  just for an opening gag or flashback and  the initial clue fans were given about  mcfarland's love of star trek peter  begins paddling around with none other  than william shatner the og captain kirk  himself unfortunately this is only a  visual cameo because shatner didn't  voice the character still it's great to  see the two interact but thanks to  stewie's weather machine makes  distracted driving takes out the show's  first real gas star my god i hit william  shatner  light growing dimmer can't breathe beam  me up god  throughout the series everyone seems to  abuse mick it's a staple of family guy  so it isn't too surprising when the  young gryffindor gets excited to make a  new friend jennifer even if she is a  little odd and too bubbly this new  friend compliments meg unlike the  cheerleaders and even invites her to  meet other people their age it seems  like a wonderful situation all around  even if the boys in the group are all  castrated meg's either so happy to have  people to finally hang out with or just  really slow but either way she misses  all of the clues that this new group  she's found is a cult the blue jumpsuit  crew is setting up to all drink some  punch and die together but thankfully  peter shows up and unwittingly saves his  daughter the kicker at the end is  peter's last line to meg after the rest  of the kids all dispose of themselves  off screen  sorry meg i guess that's another bunch  of people who'd rather fake their own  death than go to a party with you stewie  griffin is a complex individual  especially after several years of  development but he was a little easier  to follow when the character was simply  a baby evil genius in the first season  sure his oddly shaped head and  mysterious british accent might make him  seem eccentric and out of place but it's  the wild inventions and diabolical plots  that make him such a joy in those early  episodes fans will hear the full name of  this character a handful of times  throughout the series but most have  forgotten it or at least that we learned  it so early on in chitty chitty death  bang stewie's plans to fly to nicaragua  and raise an army as well as have an  in-flight happy meal are throated when  the airport staff believes him to be a  lost little boy at that point it's a  one-way trip to a security office where  the infant believes he's about to be  interrogated and that the officer works  for his enemy after an airport security  guard attempts to understand him and  offers some sound advice about growing  up stewie reveals his middle name by  stating defiantly stuart gilligan  griffin runs from nothing the evil  genius comes out a little more after  that when he thanks the guard by  freezing him and carbonite  peter griffin gets into a lot of fights  especially with ernie the giant chicken  over the years we've seen the family guy  lose his temper for various reasons and  throw down with little thought given to  his own well-being the fourth episode of  season one mind over murder shows a  great example of how his impulsive  actions get him into a ton of trouble  but this particular incident has  possibly aged the worst out of any of  the main story gags in the initial run  peter is upset that another parent is  speaking ill of his son chris calling  him moby dick among other things so  peter decides to let his frustration out  the only way he knows how with a punch  it takes a minute for peter to realize  he's hit a woman even though everyone is  calling her one the gravity of the  situation doesn't fully sink in until  she gives birth on the sidelines it's a  big plot point at the beginning of the  episode and returns later for a quick  bit but not until after peter sends her  a gift that makes things even worse  many shows resort to time travel but  that's usually when the stories are  drying up and the show has jumped the  shark family guy decided to deploy it in  its fourth episode just in case the  first three hadn't cemented that there  were no rules typical to the show's  humor time travel would be used later on  to tell full stories and set up bigger  events but in its first appearance the  science fiction element simply serves to  undo all of peter's mistakes it all  began with the teething baby stewie who  figured the best way to fight the pain  would be to speed up time things  progressed as expected on family guy  with peter punching a pregnant woman  being put on house arrest and choosing  to build a bar in his basement instead  of spending time with lois this sets up  an issue with his wife and other local  housewives who think she's taking the  attention of their men this part is also  peter's fault by singing to them at the  bar to top it off quagmire gets bored  and accidentally starts a fire on his  way out of the establishment this all  leads to stewie's time machine saving  the house from burning down by turning  back the clock and altering the past of  course this does nothing to help with  stewie's dental issues  oh my teeth  i'm free free  i claim this mouth in the name of  incisor  out of all of peter's friends joe  swanson is arguably the most interesting  of the bunch he's a superb athlete  police officer a father and a husband to  an almost constantly pregnant woman  bonnie joe does all of this as a man in  a wheelchair a fact that is hidden until  the big company softball game in his  debut episode joe is regarded as a legit  hero one who seems to get everything  right and has plenty of stories to tell  but the main one he shares in the fifth  episode a hero sits next door is the  origin of how he lost his mobility it  was a snowy christmas eve in the big  city and some presents had been stolen  from a local orphanage officer swanson  had climbed to a rooftop to find a  figure with a large sack but this  particular intruder looks familiar to  everyone as the grinch the two fought  atop the snow-covered roof and just as  joe thought he'd retrieved the  children's presence the fiendish grinch  through a skate tripping up joe and  sending him off the building the fall  paralyzed him but he found the strength  to give a christmas present to an orphan  still stewie isn't impressed with the  story and just wants to take over joe's  wheelchair oh enough if you won't share  your technological schemata with me  peaceably i shall take the information  from you by fourth wow looks like you  have a fan  lois has an odd past but most of those  aspects aren't revealed until later on  in the series and only in little bits  before things like her wealthy family or  illicit affair with a member of kiss  were brought up fans mostly saw her as  the consummate housewife the person who  had to shop cook clean and take care of  